2. Reasoning: The reader is explaining the character''s motive or emotional state (fear/caution) by citing a specific threat: falling off the bed would result in being eaten by the alligator. This goes beyond describing a physical action and delves into the character''s mental state of worry or the need to be careful to avoid a negative outcome.', 'He is so scared to fall off! Yikes, the gator is right there!', 'The reader explained that the character fears falling off his bed because an alligator would eat him. The child expressed shock at the character''s fear, noting that the alligator is right there.', '2026-10-12T04:58:41.919729+00:00', 'Why do you think the boy has to be very careful?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('ad93a2d6-d6a0-4666-8e0c-1bd4aa8ab475', '04ccfad8-0f40-43e7-92a2-88802a81f533', '7ea6c795-7dec-4e48-9815-f52043ca432e', 'P-2044', 'There used to be an alligator under my bed.', 'he must feel very scared', TRUE, 'The reader states that the character "must feel very scared," which directly attributes an emotion (fear) to the character in response to the alligator mentioned in the story text.', 'An alligator under the bed is so scary! I would hide super fast!', 'The reader noted that the character must feel very scared, and the child agreed it was scary and said they would hide super fast.', '2026-10-12T05:07:02.335772+00:00', 'How do you think the boy feels about going to bed when he believes an alligator is under there?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('6deaa65a-9115-4ab8-b50a-42776e926e04', '97876423-ac9e-438a-b998-8ed04f8d30c2', 'a353150f-1b9f-4fba-ab4f-d12f7ec54abd', 'test', 'When it was time to go to sleep, I had to be very careful because I knew he was there.', 'because if he falls off his bed the alligator will eat him', TRUE, 'The reader explains the underlying reason for the character''s caution (being "very careful") by stating a potential negative outcome: "if he falls off his bed the alligator will eat him." This reveals the character''s fear or worry about the alligator, which directly explains the thought process behind the action stated in the story text.', 'Yikes! That is so scary! He must not fall off!', 'The reader established that an alligator will eat the character if he falls off his bed. The child reacted with fear, stating that the situation is scary and emphasizing that the character must not fall.', '2026-10-12T05:08:01.841303+00:00', 'Why do you think the boy has to be very careful?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('89a2aa2c-ae4a-4891-8a79-d80d97ed3501', '97876423-ac9e-438a-b998-8ed04f8d30c2', '8176ece4-1d40-4aa8-9149-0969e0e3f3c7', 'test', 'But whenever I looked, he hid... or something. So I''d call Mom and Dad.', 'hes annoyed because his mom and dad wont belive him', TRUE, 'The reader identifies the character''s emotion ("annoyed") and explicitly provides the cognitive reason for it ("because his mom and dad wont belive him"). This involves both a feeling and an explanation of the character''s mental state.', 'He is so mad! Mom and Dad do not see it.', 'The reader explained that the character is annoyed because his parents do not believe him about the alligator. The child reacted by stating the character is very mad and noting that his parents do not see the alligator.', '2026-10-12T05:08:53.323348+00:00', 'How do you think the boy feels when he looks under the bed and can''t see the alligator?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('e1f057b3-be9c-463b-863a-9cbf682dc3c2', '97876423-ac9e-438a-b998-8ed04f8d30c2', 'ae16aaec-a265-4d5e-add6-c5b81e267aa7', 'test', 'But they never saw it. It was up to me. I just had to do something about that alligator.', 'disappointed that they dont see it ', TRUE, '1. The reader identified the feeling of "disappointment".
2. The reader explained that the character (or the "they" in the story) feels this way "that they dont see it", linking the emotion to the specific event in the text where the characters fail to notice the alligator.', 'Uh-oh, they missed the scary alligator! I feel super worried now.', 'The reader expressed disappointment that the parents do not see the alligator. The child expressed feeling super worried because they missed the scary alligator.', '2026-10-12T05:10:02.036829+00:00', 'What are Mom and Dad thinking when they look under the bed?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('8f1284c6-8576-466f-8a6f-549d4342713f', '97876423-ac9e-438a-b998-8ed04f8d30c2', '04d9981a-ec6c-4f72-95ed-1a22b2a370cf', 'test', 'So I went to the kitchen to get some alligator bait.', 'hes going to trap the alligator thats so smart', TRUE, 'The reader stated, "hes going to trap the alligator thats so smart." This includes two distinct mental state attributions. First, "hes going to trap the alligator" expresses the character''s intention or plan. Second, "thats so smart" attributes a positive cognitive evaluation or judgment to the character''s action, implying the reader thinks the character is being clever or wise. Both of these go beyond describing physical actions and reflect the character''s mind and motives.', 'He is super clever! That bait looks yummy.', 'The reader remarked that the character was smart for trapping the alligator. The child agreed the character was super clever and noted that the bait looked yummy.', '2026-10-12T05:11:29.725222+00:00', 'What is the boy planning to do with the alligator bait?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('3c9278c6-b354-4020-a5e0-5beac623e60d', 'e9334752-f277-4cd3-980b-c42378ccf645', '5cadc160-add5-4b84-b970-f0d364f7e79d', 'test', 'I put a peanut butter sandwich, some fruit, and the last piece of pie in the garage.', 'so that the room is big enough and so his family doesn''t get put in danger. hes very clever', TRUE, 'The reader states that "hes very clever," which is a cognitive state/character trait. Furthermore, the reader explains the motivation behind the action, saying he put the food in the garage so "his family doesn''t get put in danger." This expresses the character''s intention and concern for safety.', 'He is super clever! The garage keeps his family safe.', 'The reader notes that the character is clever for making the room large enough to keep his family safe from danger. The child agrees, expressing excitement that the garage keeps the family secure.', '2026-10-12T05:15:29.050565+00:00', 'Why did the boy decide to put the food all the way in the garage?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('9ec2f2f4-7902-40fe-bad1-c9c1513b6e43', 'e9334752-f277-4cd3-980b-c42378ccf645', '23ba8b6e-9aca-4496-9059-6c1daa2e2d2d', 'test', 'I put cookies down the hall. I left fresh vegetables on the stairs.', 'the alligator will get very hungry. hes a fatty', TRUE, 'The reader states that "the alligator will get very hungry," which attributes a physical state and a future intention (needing to eat) to the character. This falls under the category of desires and intentions (needs).', 'Ooh, he needs yummy cookies! Look at all his food!', 'The reader states that the alligator will become very hungry and notes that he is a fatty. The child responds by saying the alligator needs yummy cookies and observes all his food.', '2026-10-12T05:16:04.877769+00:00', 'What does the boy think the alligator will do when it sees this trail of food?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('ad691eb8-b529-498f-8384-2f08e8a40e42', 'e9334752-f277-4cd3-980b-c42378ccf645', '3b19fbbb-8122-4811-8cad-d7d3c41b9d89', 'test', 'I put a soda and some candy next to my bed. Then I watched and waited. Sure enough, out he came to get something to eat.', 'he feels anger', TRUE, 'The reader states that the character "feels anger." This is a direct attribution of an emotion to the character, which falls under the category of feelings and emotions.', 'Yikes, he looks so mad! Why is he so grumpy?', 'The reader states that the alligator feels anger. The child observes that he looks mad and grumpy, asking why he is in such a mood.', '2026-10-12T05:16:35.663437+00:00', 'How do you think the boy feels as he watches the alligator finally crawl out?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('bf2443b6-0ccc-4bcf-886d-e7c267875dc1', 'e9334752-f277-4cd3-980b-c42378ccf645', '06c2ba09-300c-42a9-bc2e-b3a4fa5c4101', 'test', 'Then I hid in the hall closet. I followed him down the stairs.', 'hes a pussy', FALSE, 'The reader simply calls the character "a pussy," which is a label or judgment of character trait (cowardice) without explicitly explaining the character''s feelings, thoughts, intentions, or reasons. It does not add commentary about why the character hid or followed, nor does it articulate the character''s internal mental state in the way MST requires.', 'Uh-oh, he is hiding! Do you think he feels scared?', 'The reader describes the alligator as "a pussy." The child observes that he is hiding and asks if he feels scared.', '2026-10-12T05:17:02.286531+00:00', 'Why did the boy hide in the closet while the alligator walked by?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('58a5348c-8098-43f1-8f42-e85206879084', 'e9334752-f277-4cd3-980b-c42378ccf645', '9373b61e-7395-486f-89c9-b8a051ef67c4', 'test', 'I followed him down the hall.', 'very happy', TRUE, '1. The reader says the character is "very happy," which explicitly identifies a feeling/emotion. 2. The reader is attributing a mental state (happiness) to the character in the story, rather than just describing the physical action of following someone down the hall.', 'I am so happy! He is walking with a big smile!', 'The reader states that the alligator is "very happy," and the child responds by asserting that the character is walking with a big smile.', '2026-10-12T05:17:19.045364+00:00', 'Why did the boy hide in the closet while the alligator walked by?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('7d4082d9-599a-4749-b04c-9ca57da9db46', 'e9334752-f277-4cd3-980b-c42378ccf645', 'e69f97d7-ca5e-43c6-b453-842f27f4d78f', 'test', 'When he crawled into the garage,', 'he hopes to trap the alligator, his plan is working verry cool!', TRUE, '1. Identify the feeling, thought, or intention the reader mentioned in response to the question. The reader attributes a specific intention and desire to the character, stating that he "hopes to trap the alligator" and that "his plan is working verry cool!" 2. Explain WHY the character feels or thinks that way according to the reader. The reader indicates that the character''s action of crawling into the garage is a deliberate attempt to achieve a goal (trapping the alligator), which involves a mental state of hoping for a specific outcome and assessing the success of his plan. This goes beyond describing a physical action by explaining the character''s motive.', 'He is being super brave! The garage is such a cool trap!', 'The reader explains that the character hopes to trap the alligator and that his plan is working well. The child responds by describing the character as super brave and identifying the garage as a cool trap.', '2026-10-12T05:17:57.050821+00:00', 'What is the boy waiting and hoping for as he hides behind the garage door?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('f7990092-4c04-4a97-bfd6-bbbd2d5e506e', 'e9334752-f277-4cd3-980b-c42378ccf645', '70359b19-798d-4f3a-a67f-6e14c8d025d3', 'test', 'I slammed the door and locked it. Then I went to bed. There wasn''t even any mess to clean up.', 'sad', TRUE, '1. The reader mentioned the feeling "sad," which is an emotion. 2. The reader identifies the character''s emotional state as "sad" in response to the events described in the story text (slamming the door, going to bed, no mess to clean up).', 'He looks so lonely in bed. Why did he slam the door?', 'The reader describes the character as sad, while the child notes he looks lonely in bed and asks why he slammed the door.', '2026-10-12T05:18:44.713887+00:00', 'How does the boy feel right after locking the alligator in the garage?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('bc5a163b-9b7e-4eaa-8069-939afee24064', 'a3e20279-c06c-4e34-bcb2-3f2b6d904d51', 'c770ea7f-d29b-4b1a-8ca7-056c5e7fab78', 'test', 'There used to be an alligator under my bed.', 'he must be very happy', TRUE, '1. The reader explicitly states the boy "must be very happy," which is a clear expression of a mental state/emotion. 2. The story context is a boy who believes there is an alligator under his bed, and the visual shows him carrying a board into his room (likely for protection). The expected emotional response is fear, worry, or being', 'Uh-oh, no! Look at his scared face. He''s worried about the alligator!', 'The child corrected the reader’s assumption of happiness by noting the character’s scared face and worry about an alligator.', '2026-11-12T09:12:54.057046+00:00', 'How do you think the boy feels about going to bed when he believes an alligator is under there?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('3b11e6c0-46a2-45e3-afc8-c937318d037e', 'a3e20279-c06c-4e34-bcb2-3f2b6d904d51', 'c44a06f5-d33d-48a7-96b2-d594f5ca6381', 'test', 'When it was time to go to sleep, I had to be very careful because I knew he was there.', 'because hes scared of the alligator', TRUE, 'The reader explicitly identifies the boy''s mental state ("scared") and the reason for it ("of the alligator"), which directly matches the expected emotion that the boy is afraid the alligator might bite him. This is a clear example of Mental State Talk (MST) as it addresses feelings and the underlying cause, and the emotion is fully', 'Uh-oh, he is so scared! Look at his wide eyes!', 'The child emphasized the character''s fear by pointing to his wide eyes. Both participants agreed that the character was scared of the alligator.', '2026-11-12T09:17:04.372271+00:00', 'Why do you think the boy has to be very careful?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('741ebbb3-6d0c-4aea-8f2f-3aecd0fefc6a', 'a3e20279-c06c-4e34-bcb2-3f2b6d904d51', 'c44a06f5-d33d-48a7-96b2-d594f5ca6381', 'test', 'When it was time to go to sleep, I had to be very careful because I knew he was there.', 'because hes scared of the alligator', TRUE, '1. The reader stated "because hes scared of the alligator," which identifies the boy''s core emotion as fear/scared. 2. This is a valid and accurate primary emotion given the context of an alligator lurking under the bed. 3. However, the expected emotion highlights a specific, more detailed nuance: the fear is specifically about the', 'Yeah, he is scared! Look at his worried eyes. Yikes, alligator bites toes!', 'The child reiterated the character''s fear by pointing to his worried eyes and noted that alligators bite toes.', '2026-11-12T09:18:44.898042+00:00', 'Why do you think the boy has to be very careful?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('1f830eb8-666f-420d-854a-b1478e7aeb49', 'bbaa3a9f-1852-4af9-b0b4-8fb96ad27815', 'c770ea7f-d29b-4b1a-8ca7-056c5e7fab78', 'test', 'There used to be an alligator under my bed.', 'he must be very happy', TRUE, '1. The reader stated the boy "must be very happy," which is a mental state (emotion) about the character, so hasMst is YES. 2. The story context is that the boy believes there is an alligator under his bed, and the question asks how he feels about going to bed knowing this. The expected emotion is fear, worry, or anxiety. 3. Saying', 'Happy? Are you sure? He looks super scared of that alligator!', 'The child redirected the reader''s assumption of happiness by noting the character''s visual appearance of being "super scared of that alligator."', '2026-11-12T09:25:33.805507+00:00', 'How do you think the boy feels about going to bed when he believes an alligator is under there?', 'INCORRECT', 'Did you ever have a scary shadow in your room when you were little?') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('ff9b607c-8910-4a26-add9-4b5837e30ecb', 'bbaa3a9f-1852-4af9-b0b4-8fb96ad27815', 'c44a06f5-d33d-48a7-96b2-d594f5ca6381', 'test', 'When it was time to go to sleep, I had to be very careful because I knew he was there.', 'he is scared of the alligator', TRUE, '1. The reader explicitly states "he is scared of the alligator," which identifies a clear fear-based emotion tied to the character''s mental state. 2. This matches the story context perfectly: the boy is terrified of the alligator under his bed and must be careful to avoid stepping on the floor where the alligator might bite him. 3. The expected emotion confirms the boy is afraid the alligator might bite his toes, so "scared" is the correct primary emotion. The reader correctly identified the core fear driving the character''s careful behavior.', 'Yikes, that is so spooky! Look at his worried face!', 'The elderly reader reaffirmed that the character is scared of the alligator. The child agreed by describing the scene as "spooky" and pointing out the character''s worried face.', '2026-11-12T09:27:28.145089+00:00', 'Why do you think the boy has to be very careful?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('06708deb-1466-465a-a84c-168031140c8a', 'bbaa3a9f-1852-4af9-b0b4-8fb96ad27815', 'c9b8c401-1d6d-4a06-a801-0b3b77d25520', 'test', 'But whenever I looked, he hid... or something. So I''d call Mom and Dad.', 'he is scared of the unknown', TRUE, '1. The reader states the boy "is scared of the unknown," which directly names a feeling (scared) and adds a cognitive element (the unknown). 2. This matches the story context: the boy is nervous/afraid of the alligator hiding under the bed and wants his parents to protect him. "Scared of the unknown" aligns well with the expected "n', 'Yikes, he is yelling for Mom! Look at that sneaky croc hiding!', 'The reader clarified that the character is scared of the unknown, while the child identified the creature as a "sneaky croc" hiding in the scene. The child also noted that the character is "yelling for Mom," adding a specific visual detail to the previous observation of the character''s worry.', '2026-11-12T09:29:18.053813+00:00', 'How do you think the boy feels when he looks under the bed and can''t see the alligator?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('68bc3cfe-e27c-42a1-8906-a96769b4fdc2', 'bbaa3a9f-1852-4af9-b0b4-8fb96ad27815', 'c9b8c401-1d6d-4a06-a801-0b3b77d25520', 'test', 'But whenever I looked, he hid... or something. So I''d call Mom and Dad.', 'he is scared of the unknown', TRUE, '1. The reader mentions "scared of the unknown," which is a feeling related to the character''s mind (MST = YES).
2. The story context shows the boy is nervous/worried because the alligator hides, and he calls his parents for protection. The expected emotion is "nervous and wants his parents to come protect him."
3. The reader''s "sc害怕', 'Yeah, he is scared! But look, he calls Mom and Dad for help!', 'The child confirmed the character is scared but redirected the focus to the character calling both Mom and Dad for help.', '2026-11-12T09:32:43.648093+00:00', 'How do you think the boy feels when he looks under the bed and can''t see the alligator?', 'PARTIAL', 'Did you ever call your mom or dad when you were scared at night?') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('3443670c-4fda-4cbb-8291-743a0dc3cd19', 'fecc8b1d-5875-4803-8efb-5c47ee0b31b2', 'c770ea7f-d29b-4b1a-8ca7-056c5e7fab78', 'P-2044', 'There used to be an alligator under my bed.', 'he must be very happy', TRUE, 'The reader states that the boy "must be very happy," which is a clear emotional attribution and therefore counts as MST. In the story, the boy believes an alligator is under his bed, which would naturally make him scared and worried, not happy. The visual context (his worried face, carrying a board defensively) and the expected-emoc', 'Happy? Are you sure? Look at his scared face, he is so worried!', 'The elderly reader suggested the character was very happy, but the child corrected this by pointing to the character''s scared face and noting he appeared worried. The child redirected the reader''s initial assumption of happiness to one of anxiety based on visual evidence.', '2026-11-12T09:34:52.866596+00:00', 'How do you think the boy feels about going to bed when he believes an alligator is under there?', 'INCORRECT', 'Did you ever have a scary shadow in your room when you were little?') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('01abe434-729a-41f8-b0c3-eb0519f3fd37', 'fecc8b1d-5875-4803-8efb-5c47ee0b31b2', 'c44a06f5-d33d-48a7-96b2-d594f5ca6381', 'P-2044', 'When it was time to go to sleep, I had to be very careful because I knew he was there.', 'because he fears the unknown. he is unsure if the alligator is under his bed so he needs to make sure but stay protected incase its true', TRUE, '1. The reader mentioned feelings and intentions: "he fears the unknown," "unsure," and "needs to stay protected." These are clearly mental-state terms, so hasMst = YES. 2. The expected emotion is that the boy is afraid the alligator will bite his toes if he steps on the floor, which is why he must be very careful. The visual scene reinforces this: he uses a board as a bridge so his feet don''t touch the floor. 3. The reader''s answer identifies the general caution and uncertainty about whether the alligator is under the bed and the need to stay protected. This aligns with the careful, fear-driven behavior, but it frames it more abstractly as "fearing the unknown" rather than the specific fear of being bitten. Because it captures a valid aspect (caution/fear) but misses the key concrete fear (bite on the toes), it is PARTIAL rather than fully CORRECT.', 'Yeah, he is careful! But look at his board feet. He is scared of bites!', 'The reader explained that the character fears the unknown and checks under the bed while staying protected. The child agreed he was careful but added that his board feet indicated a specific fear of bites.', '2026-11-12T09:35:11.004081+00:00', 'Why do you think the boy has to be very careful?', 'PARTIAL', 'What do you do when you want to feel super safe in bed?') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('947a504c-7c9f-4183-8918-98176c0b1c37', '10ad796d-beef-4604-a6d5-9be590b31f88', 'c770ea7f-d29b-4b1a-8ca7-056c5e7fab78', 'P-2044', 'There used to be an alligator under my bed.', 'he must be very happy', TRUE, 'The reader attributes happiness to the boy, which contradicts the story context where the boy is dealing with a scary alligator under his bed. The expected emotion is fear or worry.', 'Happy? Are you sure? Look at his worried face, he is super scared!', 'The reader initially assumed the character was happy, but the child corrected this by pointing to the character’s worried face as evidence that he is actually super scared.', '2026-11-12T10:13:57.8239+00:00', 'How do you think the boy feels about going to bed when he believes an alligator is under there?', 'INCORRECT', 'Did you ever have a scary shadow in your room when you were little?') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('b94e8adb-bff7-4c04-804b-36de3c288c27', '10ad796d-beef-4604-a6d5-9be590b31f88', 'c44a06f5-d33d-48a7-96b2-d594f5ca6381', 'P-2044', 'When it was time to go to sleep, I had to be very careful because I knew he was there.', 'because if he falls off his bed the alligator will eat him', TRUE, 'The reader correctly identifies the fear and the threat (alligator eating him), which aligns with the core emotional reality. However, the specific reason for being ''very careful'' in the context of the board bridge is to ensure his feet do not touch the floor where the alligator is, not necessarily to avoid falling off the bed. The reader captures the fear but misses the precise mechanical nuance of the caution described in the expected emotion.', 'Yikes, alligator is scary! But he walks on the board so his toes are safe!', 'The reader explained that the character is afraid of falling off the bed and being eaten by the alligator, and the child agreed the alligator was scary. However, the child noted that the character walks on the board, which keeps his toes safe.', '2026-11-12T10:15:03.108176+00:00', 'Why do you think the boy has to be very careful?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.session_logs (id, session_id, page_id, participation_id, story_page_text, transcript, mst_detected, mst_analysis, child_response, conversation_summary, created_at, question_text, emotion_match, follow_up_question) VALUES ('32ec9111-5eb9-4ea0-864a-29a373112c32', '10ad796d-beef-4604-a6d5-9be590b31f88', 'c9b8c401-1d6d-4a06-a801-0b3b77d25520', 'P-2044', 'But whenever I looked, he hid... or something. So I''d call Mom and Dad.', 'because he fears the unknown. he is unsure if the alligator is under his bed so he needs to make sure but stay protected incase its true', TRUE, 'The reader explicitly identifies the boy''s fear (''fears the unknown''), his cognitive state (''unsure''), and his intention/need (''needs to make sure but stay protected''). This aligns well with the expected emotion of nervousness and the desire for parental protection.', 'Yikes, he looks so scared! Look at his worried face!', 'The reader explained that the character fears the unknown and checks under the bed while staying protected in case the alligator is there. The child observed the character''s worried face and noted that he looks very scared.', '2026-11-12T10:15:19.819589+00:00', 'How do you think the boy feels when he looks under the bed and can''t see the alligator?', 'CORRECT', NULL) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
